# Leaks inside third-party libraries that the program triggers by loading its fonts: fontconfig
# keeps its pattern cache until the process ends. Not ours, and the process is ending anyway.
leak:libfontconfig

# minizip-ng (openssl backend, Linux): reading a deliberately corrupted ZIP leaks the 24-byte
# hash state that the library itself creates on its error path (unit test "a flipped byte
# anywhere never opens a wrong document"). Not ours: our own hash use (io/src/fission_file.cpp)
# creates and deletes its state in one function.
leak:mz_crypt_sha_create
